Wizard annoyances.

First off, I know this isn't reality (or is it? :)  I know things
don't always have to make sense.

Still, there are a couple of things that bug me about playing wizards.

The first is that many times a wizard will start with a spell that he
cannot use [1].  It seems to me that a newbie wizard would only know
simple or easy to cast spells.  He would not know how to cast some
riduculously hard spell, one he has almost zero chance at being
successful.  The result of this situation is that you start with an
attribute that is wasted in that you can't use it until much later in
the game, which, by the way, you may never reach.

A related situation occurred with a recent short lived wizard.  He
started with remove curse at 0% failure.  He lost the spell casting
capablity to a scroll of amnesia.  He tried to reread the spellbook to
relearn the spell but the book vanished and he was teleported across
the level.  Whazzup with that?

Another annoyance is that my barbarians (and other non-spellcasting
characters) tend not only to find numerous spellbooks but to find them
rather early in the game.  My wizards frequently find few.  Many only
find one or two more before they succumb to the YASD.

Now I know this anomoly is due to the almighty RNG.  It would take
some serious coding mojo to fix that.  But the former annoyance,
starting with a difficult spell, should be easy to fix.

Oh well ...

On to the next game.

Bill Doss

[1] I'm talking vanilla NetHack, where the wizard starts with force
bolt plus one other spell.

